  "claim": "The drummer belonged to a band called Chiefs of Relief. His band was formed in a English city. Salmon & Gluckstein were founded in this city.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Paul Cook. Sentence: Paul Thomas Cook (born 20 July 1956 in Hammersmith, London) is an English drummer and member of the punk rock band the Sex Pistols.\nPage: Sex Pistols. Sentence: The Sex Pistols were an English punk rock band formed in London in 1975.\nPage: Chiefs of Relief. Sentence: Chiefs of Relief were a British rock group with a unique electro-punk style, punctuated by the guitar work of vocalist Matthew Ashman, and also featuring drummer Paul Cook.\nPage: Salmon &amp; Gluckstein. Sentence: Founded in London in 1873 by Samuel Gluckstein and Barnett Salmon (1829-1897), they pursued an aggressive expansion to become the largest tobacco sellers in the UK, with over 140 retail outlets.",
