        "original_id": "02ebeaac-af30-5c77-b43d-3a07f9ac40a9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Cook, Matthew Ashman, Samuel Gluckstein, Barnett Salmon\n- Organizations: Sex Pistols, Chiefs of Relief, Salmon & Gluckstein\n- Places: Hammersmith, London, UK\n- Roles: Drummer, vocalist\n- Topics: Punk rock, electro-punk, tobacco retail\n\nFacts:\n- Salmon & Gluckstein was founded in London in 1873 by Samuel Gluckstein and Barnett Salmon.\n- Barnett Salmon lived from 1829 to 1897.\n- Salmon & Gluckstein expanded aggressively to become the largest tobacco seller in the UK, with over 140 retail outlets.\n- The Sex Pistols was an English punk rock band formed in London in 1975.\n- Paul Thomas Cook was born on 20 July 1956 in Hammersmith, London.\n- Paul Cook is an English drummer and a member of the Sex Pistols.\n- Chiefs of Relief was a British rock group with an electro-punk style.\n- Chiefs of Relief featured guitarist and vocalist Matthew Ashman and drummer Paul Cook.",
